  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nUpper level ridging is forecast to quickly surge in from the west\non Wednesday leaving clearing skies and lowering surface moisture\nthrough Thursday. Temperatures for the coming week will stay\nsomewhat stable across the western lower deserts, but still on\naverage slightly below normal today through Tuesday. Much cooler\ntemperatures are expected for most of Arizona with highs only in\nthe 80s for the Phoenix area Monday-Wednesday. Once the ridging\nmoves in from the west later this week, temperatures will creep\nupward again with highs topping 100 degrees across the western\ndeserts by Thursday or Friday and potentially for the Phoenix area\nby next weekend.",
